    concept:
      "Sri Lanka has no natural lakes; the \"lakes\" seen on the plain are almost all man-made reservoirs, locally called tanks or wewa. In the Dry Zone rain falls mostly in one monsoon season, and reservoirs that store wet-season water for the dry season are what keeps farming going. To understand this plain, think of \"plain plus reservoirs\" as one system.",
