      "The Adam's Peak range is built of thick charnockitic gneiss interbedded with marble and quartzite, hard rocks exposed on the main cliffs. The terrain is extremely rugged, with cliffs making up about half the area and a mean elevation of about 1,830 m. Mean annual rainfall is around 4,300 mm, and the range forms the upper catchment of the Kelani and Kalu rivers.",
