      "Mountain reserves are also \"water towers\": the Adam's Peak range gets heavy rain and has dense forest that captures rain and mist and releases it slowly into rivers, supplying the upper Kelani and Kalu in the south-west. Protecting the mountain forest means protecting water supply and flood control for the plains downstream.",
